    "created_at": "2022-10-11T15:33:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-11T15:33:14Z",
    "body": "Should autocorrection be language-dependent? How does the browser know which dictionary to use to look up words, and does it alter its triggers for lookup for  a script that doesn't use spaces, such as Chinese or Japanese or Thai (the latter has spaces but for phrase separation, rather than word), or for scripts that use different punctuation marks than English?  Is it able to tell which language a user is using when they fill in form fields if that user fills in forms in more than one language?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
