    "created_at": "2022-10-12T13:06:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-12T13:06:15Z",
    "body": "> What's the reason for not using the same behavior of inheriting from the editing host as autocapitalize does?\r\n\r\nI'm not sure, but note that `autocapitalize` doesn't reflect this in its getter. It's non-script-observable behavior. So in that sense we could always change this later if it turns out to be a problem. (The `autocapitalize` getter is worse in that it does not acknowledge URL, Email, and Password controls either. That might be something we want to try to fix, but that getter is even older so it might be high risk for little reward.)\r\n\r\n@whsieh thoughts?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
